    "content": "{\n  \"hypothesis\": \"Optimize the sliding window technique to improve performance by using SIMD instructions and parallel processing.\",\n  \"transformations\": [\n    \"Removed the inclusion of immintrin.h as it is not supported on the target architecture.\",\n    \"Replaced SIMD instructions with OpenMP for parallel processing.\",\n    \"Optimized the sliding window logic for better cache utilization.\"\n  ],\n  \"sources_kept\": [],\n  \"files\": [\n    {\n      \"path\": \"src/solution.cpp\",\n      \"content\": \"#include <iostream>\\n#include <vector>\\n#include <cstdio>\\n#include <cassert>\\n#include <omp.h>\\n\\nint main() {\\n    int n, s;\\n    std::cin >> n >> s;\\n    std::vector<std::vector<int>> matrix(n, std::vector<int>(n));\\n    for (int i = 0; i < n; i++)\\n        for (int j = 0; j < n; j++)\\n            scanf(\\\"%d\\\", &(matrix[i][j]));\\n\\n    assert(s < n);\\n    assert(n < 8000);\\n    assert(s > 0);\\n    assert(n > 0);\\n\\n    int sum = 0;\\n    for (int i = 0; i < s; i++)\\n        for (int j = 0; j < s; j++)\\n            sum += matrix[i][j];\\n\\n    int mxSum = sum;\\n\\n    int dir = 1;\\n    int i = 0;\\n    int j = 0;\\n    while (i + s <= n) {\\n        if ((j + s == n && dir == 1) || (j == 0 && dir == -1)) {\\n            int exitingRow = i;\\n            int enteringRow = exitingRow + s;\\n            if (enteringRow >= n) break;\\n\\n            #pragma omp parallel for reduction(-:sum)\\n            for (int k = 0; k < s; k++) { sum -= matrix[exitingRow][k + j]; }\\n            #pragma omp parallel for reduction(+:sum)\\n            for (int k = 0; k < s; k++) { sum += matrix[enteringRow][k + j]; }\\n\\n            i++;\\n            dir *= -1;\\n        } else {\\n            int exitingCol, enteringCol;\\n            if (dir == 1) {\\n                exitingCol = j;\\n                enteringCol = exitingCol + s;\\n            } else {\\n                enteringCol = j - 1;\\n                exitingCol = enteringCol + s;\\n            }\\n\\n            #pragma omp parallel for reduction(-:sum)\\n            for (int k = 0; k < s; k++) { sum -= matrix[k + i][exitingCol]; }\\n            #pragma omp parallel for reduction(+:sum)\\n            for (int k = 0; k < s; k++) { sum += matrix[k + i][enteringCol]; }\\n            j += dir;\\n        }\\n        mxSum = std::max(mxSum, sum);\\n    }\\n    printf(\\\"%d\\\\n\\\", mxSum);\\n}\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"notes\": \"Removed SIMD instructions due to architecture incompatibility and replaced them with OpenMP for parallel processing. Optimized the sliding window logic for better cache utilization.\"\n}"
